{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"duscope_by_type","description":"The bytes under a path in a saved scan by kind of file (video, archives, code, …), largest first, with each kind's largest files.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"duscope_by_type.input.json","title":"duscope_by_type","description":"The arguments of duscope_by_type, which runs `duscope by-type --no-scan`.","type":"object","properties":{"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The saved scan to read: an id duscope_scan or duscope_scans gave (its first 4 or more characters will do), or latest. Default: the newest saved scan that holds the path and was taken with the default options"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"A directory or file under one of the server's roots: absolute, or relative to the scan's root. Default: the scan's root, or the server's root when it has one"},"examples":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":100,"description":"The largest files listed for each kind. Default: 3"},"glob":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Only rows whose path matches one of these globs"},"exclude":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Leave out rows whose path matches one of these globs"},"size":{"type":"string","enum":["allocated","apparent"],"description":"What rows are ranked and shown by: bytes on disk (allocated, the default) or apparent length"},"fields":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z_]+$"},"description":"The fields of each row, in this order. Default: every field"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100,"description":"Rows to return. Default: 25"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}},{"name":"duscope_caches","description":"The regenerable caches under a path in a saved scan (node_modules, target, .venv, build caches, …), largest first, with what regenerates each, or one row per project; paged with cursor.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"duscope_caches.input.json","title":"duscope_caches","description":"The arguments of duscope_caches, which runs `duscope caches --no-scan`.","type":"object","properties":{"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The saved scan to read: an id duscope_scan or duscope_scans gave (its first 4 or more characters will do), or latest. Default: the newest saved scan that holds the path and was taken with the default options"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"A directory or file under one of the server's roots: absolute, or relative to the scan's root. Default: the scan's root, or the server's root when it has one"},"by_project":{"type":"boolean","description":"One row per project, the directory holding its caches' marker, instead of one per cache. Default: false"},"loose":{"type":"boolean","description":"Also list a directory named like a cache without the marker that confirms it. Default: false"},"min_size":{"type":"string","description":"Leave out caches smaller than this: 100M, 1.5G, 10KB, or a number of bytes. Default: 10M"},"size":{"type":"string","enum":["allocated","apparent"],"description":"What rows are ranked and shown by: bytes on disk (allocated, the default) or apparent length"},"fields":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z_]+$"},"description":"The fields of each row, in this order. Default: every field"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100,"description":"Rows to return. Default: 25"},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"Where the next page starts: the previous result's next_cursor, sent with the same other arguments"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}},{"name":"duscope_diff","description":"What changed between two saved scans of one tree, under a path: the entries added, removed, and grown or shrunk, largest change first, with the totals.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"duscope_diff.input.json","title":"duscope_diff","description":"The arguments of duscope_diff, which runs `duscope diff OLD NEW --under PATH`.","type":"object","properties":{"old":{"type":"string","description":"The older saved scan: an id duscope_scan or duscope_scans gave (its first 4 or more characters will do), or latest"},"new":{"type":"string","description":"The newer saved scan: an id, or latest"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"The directory both scans hold, compared under it: absolute, or relative to the older scan's root. Default: the older scan's root, or the server's root under it"},"min_delta":{"type":"string","description":"Leave out growth or shrinkage smaller than this: 100M, 1.5G, 10KB, or a number of bytes. Default: 1M"},"depth":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Compare the directories at this depth below the path whole"},"size":{"type":"string","enum":["allocated","apparent"],"description":"What is compared: bytes on disk (allocated, the default) or apparent length"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100,"description":"Rows to return. Default: 25"}},"required":["old","new"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}},{"name":"duscope_explain","description":"The facts about one file or directory: its kind and sizes, the bytes deleting it would free now (hard links and clones that keep data elsewhere left out), the cache rule it matches, and whether git ignores it; from a saved scan, or the path as it is now.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"duscope_explain.input.json","title":"duscope_explain","description":"The arguments of duscope_explain, which runs `duscope explain`.","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"The file or directory to explain, under one of the server's roots: absolute, or relative to the scan's root. Default: the scan's root, or the server's root when it has one"},"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The saved scan to read the path's totals from: an id duscope_scan or duscope_scans gave (its first 4 or more characters will do), or latest. Default: the newest saved scan that holds the path, else the path as it is now"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}},{"name":"duscope_query","description":"One read-only SQL SELECT over a saved scan's tables, which duscope_schema lists, in the command line's sandbox: 25 rows without a LIMIT, 10000 at most, 5 seconds. Reads a scan of a root or of a directory under one.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"duscope_query.input.json","title":"duscope_query","description":"The arguments of duscope_query, which runs `duscope query --no-scan --scan ID --sql SQL`.","type":"object","properties":{"sql":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"One SELECT over the scan's tables, which duscope_schema lists; :root_id and :root_last name the path's entry and the last id under it. Without a LIMIT, 25 rows; with one, at most 10000"},"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The saved scan to read: an id duscope_scan or duscope_scans gave (its first 4 or more characters will do), of a root or a directory under one. Default, or latest: the newest saved scan of a directory under the roots that holds the path"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"The entry :root_id names, under one of the server's roots: absolute, or relative to the scan's root. Default: the scan's root, or the server's root when it has one"}},"required":["sql"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}},{"name":"duscope_scan","description":"Scan a directory under the roots and save the scan: its scan_id, totals and largest directories. The other tools read saved scans, so call this first; with max_age, a recent scan of the directory is returned instead of scanning again.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"duscope_scan.input.json","title":"duscope_scan","description":"The arguments of duscope_scan, which runs `duscope scan --save`.","type":"object","properties":{"root":{"type":"string","description":"The directory to scan: absolute, under one of the server's roots. Default: the server's root when it has one"},"attrs":{"type":"string","enum":["basic","full"],"description":"The attributes to collect: full adds access and birth times, mode, owner and group, which duscope_stale's atime reads. Default: basic"},"clones":{"type":"boolean","description":"Count APFS clones once (true, the default) or every clone in full (false)"},"one_file_system":{"type":"boolean","description":"Stay on the root's filesystem. Default: false"},"max_age":{"type":"string","description":"Return a saved scan of the root taken with these options and younger than this, a number with h, d, w or y (1h), instead of scanning again. Default: always scan"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}},{"name":"duscope_scans","description":"The saved scans of directories under the roots, newest first: each one's scan_id, root, times, attributes, entry count and totals.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"duscope_scans.input.json","title":"duscope_scans","description":"The arguments of duscope_scans, which runs `duscope scans` on the server's roots: none.","type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}},{"name":"duscope_schema","description":"The index's tables and columns, for duscope_query, with each table's rows in a saved scan; or, with envelope, a verb's output as JSON Schema.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"duscope_schema.input.json","title":"duscope_schema","description":"The arguments of duscope_schema, which runs `duscope schema --scan ID`, or `duscope schema --envelope VERB`.","type":"object","properties":{"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The saved scan to read: an id duscope_scan or duscope_scans gave (its first 4 or more characters will do), of a root or a directory under one. Default, or latest: the newest saved scan of a directory under the roots that holds the path"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"A path the saved scan holds, under one of the server's roots: absolute, or relative to the scan's root. Default: the scan's root, or the server's root when it has one"},"envelope":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"A verb's name, as the result's envelopes lists them (top, stale, query, …): that verb's envelope as JSON Schema, in place of the tables"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}},{"name":"duscope_stale","description":"Large files under a path in a saved scan left unmodified for a long time (by default 10 MB and 180 days), largest first; paged with cursor.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"duscope_stale.input.json","title":"duscope_stale","description":"The arguments of duscope_stale, which runs `duscope stale --no-scan`.","type":"object","properties":{"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The saved scan to read: an id duscope_scan or duscope_scans gave (its first 4 or more characters will do), or latest. Default: the newest saved scan that holds the path and was taken with the default options"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"A directory or file under one of the server's roots: absolute, or relative to the scan's root. Default: the scan's root, or the server's root when it has one"},"older_than":{"type":"string","description":"Files left unmodified for at least this long: a number with h, d, w or y. Default: 180d"},"min_size":{"type":"string","description":"Files at least this large: 100M, 1.5G, 10KB, or a number of bytes. Default: 10M"},"atime":{"type":"boolean","description":"Also require the access time to be that old, which a scan taken with attrs full holds. Default: false"},"glob":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Only rows whose path matches one of these globs"},"exclude":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Leave out rows whose path matches one of these globs"},"size":{"type":"string","enum":["allocated","apparent"],"description":"What rows are ranked and shown by: bytes on disk (allocated, the default) or apparent length"},"fields":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z_]+$"},"description":"The fields of each row, in this order. Default: every field"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100,"description":"Rows to return. Default: 25"},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"Where the next page starts: the previous result's next_cursor, sent with the same other arguments"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}},{"name":"duscope_summary","description":"Totals under a path in a saved scan: bytes on disk and apparent, files, directories, errors, the volumes, and the bytes no entry accounts for.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"duscope_summary.input.json","title":"duscope_summary","description":"The arguments of duscope_summary, which runs `duscope summary --no-scan`.","type":"object","properties":{"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The saved scan to read: an id duscope_scan or duscope_scans gave (its first 4 or more characters will do), or latest. Default: the newest saved scan that holds the path and was taken with the default options"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"A directory or file under one of the server's roots: absolute, or relative to the scan's root. Default: the scan's root, or the server's root when it has one"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}},{"name":"duscope_top","description":"The largest directories, or files, under a path in a saved scan, largest first; narrowed by depth, size and glob, and paged with cursor.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"duscope_top.input.json","title":"duscope_top","description":"The arguments of duscope_top, which runs `duscope top --no-scan`.","type":"object","properties":{"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The saved scan to read: an id duscope_scan or duscope_scans gave (its first 4 or more characters will do), or latest. Default: the newest saved scan that holds the path and was taken with the default options"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"A directory or file under one of the server's roots: absolute, or relative to the scan's root. Default: the scan's root, or the server's root when it has one"},"files":{"type":"boolean","description":"List the largest files instead of directories. Default: false"},"depth":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"How many levels below the path to list. Default: 1 for directories, every level for files"},"min_size":{"type":"string","description":"Leave out rows smaller than this: 100M, 1.5G, 10KB, or a number of bytes"},"glob":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Only rows whose path matches one of these globs"},"exclude":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Leave out rows whose path matches one of these globs"},"size":{"type":"string","enum":["allocated","apparent"],"description":"What rows are ranked and shown by: bytes on disk (allocated, the default) or apparent length"},"fields":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z_]+$"},"description":"The fields of each row, in this order. Default: every field"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100,"description":"Rows to return. Default: 25"},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"Where the next page starts: the previous result's next_cursor, sent with the same other arguments"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}},{"name":"test_summary","description":"A saved scan's totals under a path (a test fixture).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"A path under a root"},"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"latest, or a saved scan's id"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}},{"name":"test_top","description":"The largest directories under a path (a test fixture).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100}},"required":["path"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/maxResultSizeChars":24000}}],"ttlMs":3600000,"cacheScope":"public","resultType":"complete","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"duscope","version":"<version>"}}}}
